{
  "review": "See docs/handoff/security-2026-09/client-lifetime.html for input/result categories, uncached operations and local state ownership. Every changed mutation-capable module requires renewed sensitivity review. Self-configuration preparation and rollout review retain only revision, generation, request ID and plan digest metadata; factor codes remain in sensitive local state and factor responses bypass mutation caches. Hashes were re-pinned after merging origin/main: the design-system migration (routes moved onto the shared ui primitives Dialog/Menu/Alert/Button/Select and helpers) and the react/set-state-in-effect refactor (resets moved from effects to useResetOnChange, seeded useState, or key-based remounts) both changed module bytes without adding a mutation surface, cache boundary, or plaintext ownership. Literal NUL bytes accidentally written into signature template literals were replaced with the \\u0000 escape (no runtime change). The sensitivity posture is unchanged. The login challenge passkey leg (api/stepup useLoginChallengePasskey) mirrors usePasskeyLogin: no cache, no retained result. The sign-in enrolment gate (#785, routes/EnrolmentGate + ui/auth/SecondFactorSetup) holds the re-proved password in component sensitive state until it is handed to the recovery-code mutation, whose guarded account-session transfer carries it with the codes across that one remint (retirement would otherwise wipe it) so the factor enrolment that follows can present it; the gate releases the password once an authenticator enrolment starts, and both die with the gate. useRegenerateRecoveryCodes and the gate share one handoff (useRecoveryCodeHandoff). Storybook coverage pass (feat/storybook-coverage): routes/MachineAccess and routes/ScimProvisioning changed by `export` keywords only (page, dialog and card components) so stories can mount them; no mutation surface, cache boundary or plaintext ownership changed.",
